Z||000000||CozmoPooky||02-24-2001||01:06 PM||||Finally happened<BR>Going over to Old Town for a wide track Pontiac show with some club members the ole Duke gave up the ghost.  80 MPH cruzin' along fine than nothing- just like the ignition was shut off. Coasted to a stop on I-4 (where all the fires are now in Florida). Naturally I was "tail end charlie" so the rest of the pack just kept on truckin, I bet they wonder what happened to me...<BR>Checked the car lots of fuel, spark than pulled off the oil filler cap and cranked it over...the little valve thingies WEREN'T MOVING! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  I guess the timing gears are toast. Got a tow home, AAA is great!<BR>How tough is it to fix?  The book says you can change them in the car, but since I was going to put a 4.9 Caddy engine in anyway I think I won't even try to fix the Duke.<BR>So this means the Caddy project is now front burnered! This should be an interesting adventure...<P>------------------<BR>Cozmo<BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>'87 Duke Coupe     <BR>'85 2M6 Targa<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bothfierossig1.jpg"> ||||reg||11
